# Feature delivery rule

Use this checklist before declaring a feature complete. It complements `core.mdc`, `documentation.mdc`, and `adr.mdc`.

## Definition of done

1. **Code**
   - Build succeeds; **no new compiler warnings** in files this change adds or modifies (`build-warnings.mdc`).
   - Async with `CancellationToken` on I/O in Infrastructure.
   - Keep orchestration and parsing in Infrastructure/Core; TrayApp stays thin.

2. **Tests** (default: include in the same change — see `testing.mdc`)
   - New or changed logic in Core/Infrastructure has unit tests in `BuildMonitor.Tests`.
   - UI-only XAML: document manual checks in the feature doc when tests are N/A.
   - Existing tests still pass.

3. **Documentation**
   - `docs/features/<file>.md` added or updated for user-facing changes.
   - **Behaviour section** (see `documentation.mdc`) when the change has non-obvious pipeline logic (orchestrator, process output parsing, port probing).
   - [`docs/SETTINGS.md`](../../docs/SETTINGS.md) when settings schema changes.
   - [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) when orchestration or project layout changes.
   - [`docs/LOGS.md`](../../docs/LOGS.md) when log format or storage changes.
   - [`docs/README.md`](../../docs/README.md) index updated when a top-level doc was added.
   - [`README.md`](../../README.md) when developer setup steps change.

4. **ADR** (only when a lasting decision was made)
   - New ADR under `docs/adr/NNNN-title.md` from `0001-template.md`.
   - Or existing ADR superseded with forward/back links.

5. **Security**
   - No secrets, PATs, or user settings in committed files.
   - New config keys documented in `docs/SETTINGS.md` only.

6. **PR**
   - PR description follows [`.github/pull_request_template.md`](../../.github/pull_request_template.md) and links the issue (`Closes #N`).

## Triggers requiring an ADR

Add an ADR when the change introduces or changes:

- Settings schema version or persistence location
- Child process launch / environment isolation strategy
- Log storage format or retention
- A major refactor of orchestrator boundaries

## Drift-check anchors

When you touch these, expect documentation updates in the same change:

- `src/Infrastructure/Services/ProjectOrchestrator.cs`
- `src/Infrastructure/LocalBuild/DotNetProcessConfigurator.cs`
- `src/Core/Settings/LocalAppSettings.cs`
- `src/TrayApp/SettingsWindow.xaml.cs`
- `docs/SETTINGS.md`
